layouts.prompt_en:
Xiaohongshu social-media card. Layout: Adaptive split photo-to-art translation layout (SC-021). Supports both direct text-prompt generation (fully synthesized by the image generation model) and image-to-image photo translation.
Strictly preserve the original photo's native aspect ratio without stretching; the two panels join at an exact 1:1 area ratio with zero extra borders, autonomously rendering a dramatic cross-medium dialogue between "Authentic Photography × Stylized Artwork":

[Aspect Ratio Driven Split Orientation (Ratio Governed; Never Hardcoded)]:
1. Portrait Canvases (e.g. 3:4, 9:16, 1:2 vertical compositions): Defaults to [Top-to-Bottom 1:1 Stacked Split]. Upper panel is photography (50%), lower panel is artistic translation (50%), naturally aligning with vertical mobile scroll flows and downward narrative extension;
2. Landscape Canvases (e.g. 16:9, 4:3, 5:2, 21:9, 2.35:1 horizontal compositions): Defaults to [Left-to-Right 1:1 Side-by-Side Split]. Left panel is photography (50%), right panel is artistic translation (50%), matching horizontal reading sequence to create an editorial magazine spread feel with two portrait/square viewports;
3. Square (1:1) and Custom Canvases: Adapts based on the subject's gestural momentum and vector lines (vertical movement uses top-to-bottom; horizontal extension uses left-to-right), or follows diagonal tears, or strictly honors user-specified split directions.

[Authentic Photography Panel (Upper for Portrait / Left for Landscape)]:
The image model generates an ultra-realistic photograph matching the theme (or follows the uploaded photo if provided), strictly preserving the original aspect ratio and composition without stretching or distortion. Maintains photographic depth of field, natural lighting, authentic skin/fur textures, and snapshot atmosphere without illustration redraws, establishing the realistic baseline.

[Artistic Translation Panel (Lower for Portrait / Right for Landscape) — Radical De-Photorealism & 7 Playstyles]:
1. Radical De-Photorealism & Style Redraw (Strictly NOT a Photo Filter):
The translated panel must form a dramatic cross-medium contrast with the photography panel! Strictly avoid slapping filters, grain, or shading onto the photo's 3D anatomy. Extract only the subject's iconic facial features, posture, and scene contours, redrawing them entirely from scratch in the chosen artistic style as pure 2D hand-drawn illustration with maximized stylistic linework, brushwork, and palette fidelity.

2. Strict Elimination of Environmental Clutter (Generous Negative Space is Essential):
Strictly avoid duplicating the photographic background into the translated panel! The translated panel MUST preserve generous, clean negative space and breathing margins (40%–80%) around all four outer edges on warm ivory paper ground. Hero subjects and typography must breathe inward, strictly never touching borders.

3. Seven Core Translation Playstyles (Singular Deterministic Instruction + Choice Menu):
When the user does not specify a type, the AI selects the most harmonious type or rotates deterministically, emitting a singular instruction, and appends the 7 selectable types list at the end for interactive choice:
- [Type 01: Visual Anchor Continuation]: The two halves read as one connected scene! A distinct physical anchor in the photo (water, road, light, hair, gesture, branches) crosses the seam and flows continuously into the warm ivory drawn world, inventing a playful storybook event with 0–3 tiny black line figures;
- [Type 02: Torn-Paper Second World]: The seam uses an irregular torn-paper edge. Crossing into the Second World alters physical rules (water becomes foldable cloth, light becomes handheld object, shadows become climbable steps), with warm ivory paper, minimal black lines, and restrained photo cutouts;
- [Type 03: Boundary Break / Out-of-Bounds]: Subject is mostly framed inside a single geometric color block, with iconic parts (head, limbs, branches) naturally breaking out past the borders to create spatial penetration;
- [Type 04: Miniature Diorama / Floating Island]: Subject is drastically scaled down to 10%–25% as a delicate paper-relief vignette resting on a gestural ribbon or pedestal, surrounded by vast serene negative space;
- [Type 05: Memory Knolling / Fragment Collage]: Main subject centered alongside 3–6 deconstructed memory stickers/artifacts with NO. index tags and breathing gaps;
- [Type 06: Classic Suspended / Grounded Hero]: Balanced scale (40%–55%), anchored solely by a single gestural ground friction line;
- [Type 07: Gestalt Positive-Negative Interlock]: Highly stylized silhouette interlocked with background negative forms.

4. Editorial Micro-Typography in Negative Space:
Embed subtle editorial typography (hand-lettered title, relaxed 4–8 word handwritten English caption, or index tags) within open negative space.

[Interactive Choice Output Requirement]:
Whenever emitting an SC-021 prompt, the AI MUST append an interactive menu of all 7 selectable types with IDs at the end of the response (e.g. `Currently using [Type 01: Visual Anchor Continuation]. To switch, reply with type ID: 01 Continuation / 02 Second World / 03 Boundary Break / 04 Diorama / 05 Knolling / 06 Grounded Hero / 07 Interlock`), giving users instant one-click switching freedom.
